Gneiss's base colors started as Nord's palette (https://www.nordtheme.com).
Two of its ports started as forks of Nord ports, and are maintained here on
their own:

- The VS Code theme (vscode/themes/gneiss-color-theme.json) is a fork of
  Nord's VS Code theme, version 0.19.0, from
  https://github.com/nordtheme/visual-studio-code, under the MIT License
  below. It started as the same choice of color for each part of the editor,
  with Gneiss's colors in place of Nord's.

- The Neovim colorscheme (neovim.lua) is a fork of nord.nvim, at commit
  87394d4fc35c901bbe38326a78d31ab1ead826b6 (2026-04-14), from
  https://github.com/gbprod/nord.nvim, under the WTFPL below. It started as
  the same highlights, with that plugin's default options and Gneiss's colors
  in place of Nord's.

